Dear Kenneth,

I realized that I screwed up the example (since ^ coerces to real anyway).

The general point is that if at least one number in a computation is real, 
then integers that enter into the computation will be coerced to real. 
Here's a valid example:

        > cube <- function(x) (as.double(x))*x*x
        > cube(5000)
        [1] 1.25e+011
        >

(I guess that it's too early in the morning for me to think clearly.)

Sorry,
 John

