G'day Sven,

>>>>> "SK" == Sven Knudsen <Sven.Knudsen at adeptscience.dk> writes:

    SK> I would like to add to formula objects : for example,

    SK> form1 <- y~F1 form2 <- ~F2

    SK> where F1 and F2 are two factors, and y is the response
    SK> (double). [...]  Any suggestions?
Which S-Plus version?  Bill Venables came up with a merge.formula()
function for a package that we once developped.  That was for S-Plus
3.4 and in your case the code is essentially:

    > str <- paste(c(deparse(form1[[2]]), "~",
    + deparse(form1[[3]]), "+",
    + deparse(form2[[length(form2)]])), collapse="")
    > str
    [1] "y~F1+F2"
    > as.formula(str)
    y ~ F1 + F2
    > form3 <- as.formula(str)
    > form3
    y ~ F1 + F2

That works for me on S-Plus 5.1 (under Linux).  Don't know about
S-Plus 6.

Hope that helps.

Cheers,

        Berwin

