From ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk  Fri Oct 18 21:06:35 2002
From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk
Date: Fri, 18 Oct 2002 22:06:35 +0100
Subject: Re: problem with S_alloc on Windoze
In-Reply-To: <51F9C42DA15CD311BD220008C707D81906FFC7CB@usrymx10.merck.com>
References: <51F9C42DA15CD311BD220008C707D81906FFC7CB@usrymx10.merck.com>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.31.0210182157110.13523-100000@gannet.stats>

Probably a header problem, which resulted in not declaring the entry point
S_alloc as stdcall (and not the default cdecl).  The wrong calling type
causes stack corruption, usually after around 20 calls ....

Perhaps we had better explore offline exactly what you are doing, but a
quick thing to try is the -mrtd flag mentioned in those complements.

